    "research": {
      "notes": "**Scope:** I found almost nothing dated 2026-09-14 to 2026-10-14. The items below are the in-window findings, followed by recent items just outside the window for context.\n\n## 1. Guidance\n- No guidance change, pre-announcement or Q3 results found in the window. Nothing material.\n- Outside the window: \nTIC reported Q2 on 2026-08-06 and reaffirmed its full-year 2026 outlook.\n — 2026-08-06 — https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/0002032966/000162828026053818/ticsolutions-x2q26earnings.htm\n- Q3 guide: \nrevenue of $610M–$630M and adjusted EBITDA of $100M–$110M.\n — 2026-08-06 — https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/08/13/tic-solutions-tic-q2-2026-earnings-call-transcript/\n- FY2026 guide: \n$2.15B–$2.25B revenue and $330M–$355M adjusted EBITDA.\n — 2026-08-06 — https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/08/13/tic-solutions-tic-q2-2026-earnings-call-transcript/\n- Q2 versus expectations: \nadjusted EPS of $0.10 against a $0.36 forecast.\n — 2026-08-06 — https://www.investing.com/news/transcripts/earnings-call-transcript-tic-solutions-posts-q2-2026-eps-miss-as-backlog-grows-93CH-4842740\n- Another source puts Q2 consensus at \n$0.10 on $584.35M revenue.\n The snippet is truncated, so I can't tell what the $0.10 refers to. — date unknown — https://www.perplexity.ai/finance/TIC\n- I did not find the Q3 earnings date.\n\n## 2. Analyst actions\n- No rating or price-target change was found dated within the window. Nothing material.\n- Outside the window, per Finviz: \nJP Morgan upgraded Underweight to Neutral with a $11 target on Aug-21-26, and UBS upgraded Neutral to Buy with a $12.50 target on Aug-11-26.\n — 2026-08-21 and 2026-08-11 — https://finviz.com/stock?t=TIC\n- Yahoo Finance shows the JP Morgan move as \na price target raise from 9 to 11.\n — 2026-08-21 — https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/TIC/\n- Consensus figures differ by aggregator:\n  - \nAverage target $11.57, consensus \"Buy\" (StockAnalysis).\n — date unknown — https://stockanalysis.com/stocks/tic/statistics/\n  - \nTarget $12.25 (Finviz).\n — date unknown — https://finviz.com/stock?t=TIC\n\n## 3. Litigation and regulation\n- No lawsuits, investigations, fines or regulatory actions involving TIC Solutions were found in the window. Nothing material.\n- Search hits for \"TIC\" were unrelated entities: TIC International data-breach suits, tenants-in-common investments, and a 2000s EEOC case against TIC the Industrial Company. I did not attribute these to TIC Solutions.\n\n## 4. Customer concentration and contracts\n- No customer wins, losses or concentration disclosures found in the window. Nothing material.\n- Outside the window: \nmanagement said it was awarded multiple new run-and-maintain sites and new awards supporting client capital projects.\n — 2026-08-06 — https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/08/13/tic-solutions-tic-q2-2026-earnings-call-transcript/\n- Q2 commentary also cited \n2025 site losses and shifted outage timing\n in Inspection & Mitigation. — 2026-08-06 — same URL.\n- I did not review the 10-K for concentration figures.\n\n## 5. Insider activity\n- CFO Kristin Schultes: \n60,000 performance-based RSUs converted to common stock, and 18,624 shares were disposed of under code F (tax withholding) at $8.32.\n That left 48,316 shares held directly. This is not an open-market sale. — 2026-09-30 — https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/0002032966/000121390026106422/ownership.xml\n- StockTitan notes \nno Rule 10b5-1 plan is reported\n for that filing. — 2026-09-30 — https://www.stocktitan.net/sec-filings/TIC/form-4-tic-solutions-inc-insider-trading-activity-cfc491cd5384.html\n- An aggregator shows \n10 insider buys and 9 sales ($155K sold) in the past 90 days.\n The $155K matches the CFO's tax-withholding value, so it likely is not open-market selling. I could not verify the \"buys.\" — date unknown — https://www.athenic.com/finance/TIC\n- I found no clustered selling and no open-market purchases in the